# One row wrong in every way a per-row check can catch, seeded literally because no verb
# would write it. The point is the *order* the complaints come back in: identity against
# the file, then values against the vocabulary, then the (status, closed, resolution)
# unit, then custom fields. Nothing else pins that, so a refactor of the row checks could
# reshuffle a user's error report and every other fixture would still pass.
